  "question": {
    "text": "The half-life of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Au</mi><mn>198</mn></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn></math> days. The activity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mg</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Au</mi><mn>198</mn></msup></math>, if its atomic weight is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>198</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>"
